=== stdout ===
OptiForge 0.1.0 - a profile-guided optimizing compiler

usage: optiforge <input.of> [options]

Output:
  -o <file>            Write output to <file>
  --emit=<stage>       Stop after <stage> and dump its result
                       (tokens, ast, ir, cfg, asm, obj)

Optimization:
  -O0                  No optimization (default)
  -O1                  Basic optimization
  -O2                  Full optimization
  --regalloc=<kind>    Register allocator: naive or graph (default: graph)

Profiling:
  --profile            Build an instrumented binary that writes a .prof
  --profile-out=<file> Where that binary writes it (default: <output>.prof)
  --profile-time       Also record per-function wall time
  --use-profile=<file> Compile against a profile collected earlier
  --profile-report=<f> Print a hot-path report for <f> and exit
  --hot-threshold=<%>  Cumulative share that defines hot (default: 80)

Diagnostics:
  -Werror              Treat warnings as errors

General:
  -h, --help           Show this message
      --version        Show the version
